{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178889-familiar-addition","id":1178889,"title":"Familiar Addition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-24T11:50:30-08:00","id":1178889,"title":"Familiar Addition","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> So I have a character that is looking to spend some XP on the Familiar merit, but they do not have the power to grant themselves one and I got to thinking about the different avenues the character could take to get this goetia familiar. Below are my methods:<br /> <br /> #1. Summon a Supernal Being to grant one (not sure on Rank Requirements)<br /> #2. Get a powerful NPC to help with the binding<br /> #3. Travel to the Astral Realms and have a powerful spirit make the bond<br /> <br /> What do you guys think would be some good alternatives or methods to grant this familiar?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T13:10:20-08:00","id":1178910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178889-familiar-addition#post1178889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> So I have a character that is looking to spend some XP on the Familiar merit, but they do not have the power to grant themselves one and I got to thinking about the different avenues the character could take to get this goetia familiar. Below are my methods:<br /> <br /> #1. Summon a Supernal Being to grant one (not sure on Rank Requirements)<br /> #2. Get a powerful NPC to help with the binding<br /> #3. Travel to the Astral Realms and have a powerful spirit make the bond<br /> <br /> What do you guys think would be some good alternatives or methods to grant this familiar?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Familiar Spell is Spirit 4. So a Supernal would need to be Rank 4, an NPC have Spirit 4, etc. They'd also need to sink enough Mana/Reach to make it Lasting (I'd think), and probably Relinquish it (safely, hopefully).<br /> <br /> Or, you could do what I do - Some Ephemerals have it as a Manifestation, rules and text to the contrary be damned.<br /> <hr /><br /> Side note: I first saw this and thought it said &quot;Familiar Addi<u><b>c</b></u>tion&quot;. Like, someone either needs to be hooked up to a Familiar, or just <i>has</i> to keep adding more. I remember someone once posited that maybe Solomon (of yore) was a Mage that bound a truly <i>massive</i> number of spirits to them as Familiars (maybe sustained by 1K or so Sleepwalker wives holding the Familiar spells?). Of course, if you took your time (and sunk XP into reclaiming the Willpower Dots due to safe Relinquishment), you wouldn't need the Sleepwalkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-24-2018, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T13:25:24-08:00","id":1178914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178889-familiar-addition?p=1178910#post1178910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Familiar Spell is Spirit 4. So a Supernal would need to be Rank 4, an NPC have Spirit 4, etc. They'd also need to sink enough Mana/Reach to make it Lasting (I'd think), and probably Relinquish it (safely, hopefully).</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit isn\u2019t required to get a goetic familiar, also you can\u2019t make Familiar a Lasting effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T13:51:54-08:00","id":1178923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178889-familiar-addition?p=1178914#post1178914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirit isn\u2019t required to get a goetic familiar, also you can\u2019t make Familiar a Lasting effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Substitute Death 4 or Mind 4 (for Ghosts and Goetia, respectively), yes. General point still stand regarding capabilities. Indefinite, whatever (stupid similar terms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:24:59-08:00","id":1178991,"title":"","content":"It still feels odd that the familiar merit by the rules is still controlled by someone though that fits with how the Merit can be ended. It'd be nice if it was able to be a lasting effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:50:14-08:00","id":1179005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178889-familiar-addition?p=1178991#post1178991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still feels odd that the familiar merit by the rules is still controlled by someone though that fits with how the Merit can be ended. It'd be nice if it was able to be a lasting effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shrug&gt; That's why I just let some ephemerals have it and go with &quot;Mages are able to force it&quot;.<br /> <br /> I <i>want</i> to be able to have the odd Ghost/Goetic/Spirit bond with even a mortal, without Mage interference needed. The story concept is just too useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:56:30-08:00","id":1179009,"title":"","content":"I supposse there are always exceptions to the rule. This one hereditary Familiar from Night Horrors: The Unbidden is a perfect candidate for having developed the Manifestation on its own, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T05:55:39-08:00","id":1179165,"title":"","content":"If you happen to have Mind/Death/Spirit 3 and you don't mind going on a quest for it, you could journey through the Astral Realms and visit the Aeons. With the Auctoritas Arcanum (treat an arcanum as 1 dot higher for 1 spell) you can create the familiar bond yourself, without buying the merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23592-aurelius","name":"Aurelius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}